==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|zickīn|lang=goh}} ‘female kid’, from {{proto|Germanic|tikk-īn-|lang=de}} (compare Old English {{term|ticcen|lang=ang}} ‘kid’), from {{proto|Indo-European|digós|lang=de}} ‘goat’, genitive of {{proto|Indo-European|title=|díks|lang=sq}}. More at {{l|de|Ziege}}.

===Noun===
{{de-noun|g=f|plural=Zicken}}
# [[she-goat]], [[nanny goat]]
# [[bitch]] (arrogant woman)

